  "result": "Race condition from non-atomic read-modify-write. Two requests read same value, both increment, both write \u2014 one increment lost.\n\n**Fix: atomic SQL update**\n\n```sql\nUPDATE counters\nSET value = value + 1\nWHERE id = $1\nRETURNING value;\n```\n\nSingle round-trip, no separate read. PostgreSQL row-level lock handles concurrency.\n\n**Node.js (pg):**\n```js\nconst { rows } = await pool.query(\n  'UPDATE counters SET value = value + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING value',\n  [counterId]\n);\nreturn rows[0].value;\n```\n\nNo transaction needed for single-row atomic increment. If multiple rows involved, wrap in `BEGIN/COMMIT`.",
